    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "addrman: don't stall feelers when a tried collision is unreachable",
    "user": {
      "login": "naiyoma",
      "id": 40592031,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQwNTkyMDMx",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40592031?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/naiyoma",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/naiyoma/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "When the old entry in a collision is unreachable and hasn't connected successfully in the last 4 hours, it can only leave the collision set through the 40-minute `ADDRMAN_TEST_WINDOW` branch. Until then, if it's the only pending collision, no feeler connections are made at all.\nThis is a rare occurrence I ran into when I switched from dual-homed (IPv4 + Tor) to `-onlynet=ipv4`.\n\n`ThreadOpenConnections()` repeatedly calls `SelectTriedCollision()`, which keeps returning the unreachable entry. Since its network is unreachable, the entry is skipped without making a connection. `nTries` eventually runs out without any feeler connections being made.\nThe same process repeats on subsequent feeler turns until `ResolveCollisions()` resolves the collision after `ADDRMAN_TEST_WINDOW` (40 minutes).\n\nThis PR passes the reachable networks to `SelectTriedCollision()`, so it only returns collisions whose to-be-evicted entry belongs to a reachable network.\nIf none of the pending collisions qualify, nothing is returned, and a regular feeler connection is made instead.\n\nAnother approach I considered [2](https://github.com/naiyoma/bitcoin/pull/25) is to overwrite unreachable tried entries involved in a collision directly in `ResolveCollisions()`. \n",
